{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1139463-2e-bloodline-like-cappadocians-from-vtm","id":1139463,"title":"[2E] Bloodline like Cappadocians from VtM","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-11T09:13:13-07:00","id":1139463,"title":"[2E] Bloodline like Cappadocians from VtM","content":"I run a Viking Werewolf game and want to send my PC to Byzantine Empire. I think about story set in Cappdocia\u2019s monastery, so what would be better than necromancy using vampires in there? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> To the point \u2013 <b>As I like VtM Cappadocians Clan concept, I would want using similar Bloodline in my WtF game. </b>If there is nothing similar in official VtR canon, we could recreate Cappadocians as Bloodline.<b> I would think they would be from Mekhet Clan, but I\u2019m totally empty how to make their necromantic magic as Discipline</b>. I would also assume they would be strong on Postmortem Embrace, on general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-30-2018, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T11:51:43-07:00","id":1139502,"title":"","content":"Maybe Bloodline isn't the right path...<br /> <br /> What about a Cappadocian Covenant being a Death focused Covenant that uses Necromancy as outlined in this post:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615801-necromancy-as-blood-sorcery?p=833876#post833876\">Link</a><br /> <br /> ?<br /> <br /> That'd allow greater diversity among the Necromancers, and it does seem more like a significant philosophical schism that would distinguish it from other Covenants than a niche Bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-11-2017, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T14:13:14-07:00","id":1139547,"title":"","content":"That depends on the path. I'd fit them in with the Lancea et Sanctum, but give some Ordo Dracul style practices.<br /> <br /> <u>Corpse in the Monster</u><br /> Now this is a Mystery, like something that the Ordo Dracul would develop. Unlike the Ordo Dracul, Cappodocians believe that they're sanctified, that their undead state given to them by God is something to be celebrated and they do that by studying it. In doing so, they have learnt ways of enjoying the benefits of life and death beyond that of ordinary vampires. More ascetic vampires are suspicious of these developments. Less ascetic vampires (like most of Invictus) often appreciate their talents.<br /> <br /> <u>Cadaverous Animation</u><br /> They study a form of vitalism, concerned with the power of vitae and can use it to animate and control corpses or parts of corpses. Most vampires consider this to be a strange, disturbing and <i>nonconstructive</i> use of one's requiem. It can be used to create unfeeling war ghouls, but princes tend not to appreciate their subjects raising private zombie armies. As such, these Cappodocians keep their distance from other vampires.<br /> <br /> <u>The Grave's Decay</u><br /> These Cappodocians are unnatural ascetics who learn to endow their vitae with necrotic properties (including aggravated damage). They use this in combat and to punish the living and dead, often in poetic ways for different types of sin. They're a pillar of the Lancea et Sanctum and they're hated and feared. What they know don't is that they're using a rather simple form of Cruac.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T14:46:14-07:00","id":1139556,"title":"","content":"You may like these then:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/781660-bloodline-lazarenes#post781660\">Lazarenes</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1099206-the-stygians-fan-bloodline#post1099206\">Stygians</a> (these are even listed as associated with the Lance)<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bwe_U8ZCU4OudhtOodunsg3KS3WAFom5uCvYnG1fgo8/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Sangiovanni</a> with their<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kvV1IuBPaMZQ5DMTySP02hxoNYNbg1xbBBMi47v2uSg/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Cattivera</a><br /> <br /> I am just linking things listed in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub#post8627\">Requiem Homebrew Hub</a>, I'd suggest take a look yourself, there are great things in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-11-2017, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T15:32:23-07:00","id":1139563,"title":"","content":"I think there are also the ... Osites from the lancea sanctum book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}